  "result": "I fixed the bug in `IntRange._clamp` in `src/click/types.py`. `tests/test_types.py` passes (41 passed, 2 skipped).\n\nFor an open boundary, the method returned `bound - dir`, which moves the wrong way. `dir` is `1` when clamping up from `min` and `-1` when clamping down from `max`. So a value below an open `min` was clamped to `min - 1`, and a value above an open `max` to `max + 1`. Both are outside the allowed range. It now returns `bound + dir`, so the result lands on the nearest valid integer inside the range.\n\nI didn't add a regression test for the open-boundary case.",
